+# USDC Pay
+
+A minimal dApp for sending **USDC on Ethereum mainnet**. Connect a wallet, see
+your USDC and ETH balances, enter a recipient and amount, and send.
+
+- **`/pay`** — the whole app. The root route redirects here.
+- USDC token: [`0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48`](https://etherscan.io/token/0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48)
+
+## Stack
+
+- **Next.js** (App Router) + **TypeScript**
+- **wagmi v2** + **viem v2** for chain reads/writes
+- **RainbowKit** for wallet connection
+- **TanStack Query** (wagmi's data layer)
+- **Tailwind CSS**
+
+## Getting started
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # add a WalletConnect project id
+npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000  → redirects to /pay
+```
+
+### Environment
+
+| Variable | Required | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` | For WalletConnect / mobile wallets | Free id from [Reown/WalletConnect Cloud](https://cloud.reown.com). Injected wallets (MetaMask, Rabby) work without it. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC_URL` | Recommended for production | A dedicated mainnet RPC (Alchemy/Infura). Falls back to a public RPC. |
+
+## How it works
+
+- **Balances** — reads `decimals`, `symbol` and `balanceOf` straight from the
+  USDC contract (batched via multicall) and the account's native ETH balance.
+  Both refetch automatically once a transfer confirms.
+- **Sending** — calls the ERC-20 `transfer(recipient, amount)` on USDC. The
+  amount is parsed with the token's real decimals.
+
+### USDC details handled faithfully
+
+- **6 decimals, not 18.** Amounts are parsed with `parseUnits(amount, 6)`, and
+  the input rejects more than 6 fractional digits. Decimals are read from the
+  contract at runtime rather than assumed.
+- **Checksummed address**, validated at module load via viem's `getAddress`.
+- **Mainnet-only.** The app is locked to chain id 1; on any other network it
+  prompts the user to switch before showing balances or the form.
+
+## Validation & UX
+
+- Recipient must be a valid Ethereum address (with a gentle warning when it's
+  your own address).
+- Amount must be a positive number within your USDC balance and within 6
+  decimals; a **Max** button fills your full balance.
+- ETH balance is shown because you need it for gas, with a warning when it's zero.
+- Full transaction lifecycle: *confirm in wallet → submitted → confirmed*, with
+  an Etherscan link and readable error messages (including user rejections).
+
+## Project structure
+
+```
+app/
+  layout.tsx        # root layout + providers
+  providers.tsx     # wagmi + RainbowKit + React Query
+  page.tsx          # redirects to /pay
+  pay/page.tsx      # the pay screen (connect, network guard, balances, form)
+components/
+  Balances.tsx      # USDC + ETH balance tiles
+  PayForm.tsx       # recipient/amount form + send lifecycle
+lib/
+  wagmi.ts          # mainnet-only wagmi config
+  usdc.ts           # USDC address + ERC-20 ABI
+  useUsdcAccount.ts # balances + token metadata hook
+  format.ts         # amount parsing/formatting helpers
+```
+
+## Notes
+
+- Not audited; test with small amounts. ERC-20 transfers are irreversible — a
+  wrong recipient means lost funds. The app validates address format but cannot
+  verify you typed the *right* address.
